      "excerpt": "BC-24V-USA \u2013 HUDSON ELECTRONICS UK Skip to navigation Skip to content Search for: Search Menu PEDALS BROADCAST AP-II BROADCAST BROADCAST \u2013 dual foot switch MOTORCYCLE SIDECAR BROADCAST-AP BROADCAST LIMITED EDITIONS BROADCAST-AP / Green Limited Edition BROADCAST-AP / Blue Limited Run PG-24V-FS \u2013 rosso corsa BC-24V-USA PG-24V-FS \u2013 magenta PG-24V-FS \u2013 mint turquoise BC-24V-PG BC-24V-LTD STOCKISTS SOUNDS SUPPORT FAQs INTERNAL TRIMMERS POWER REQUIREMENTS WARRANTY PRIVACY POLICY WEEE Policy CONTACT CUSTOM ARCHIVED Home PEDALS BROADCAST AP-II BROADCAST BROADCAST \u2013 dual foot switch MOTORCYCLE SIDECAR BROADCAST-AP BROADCAST LIMITED EDITIONS BROADCAST-AP / Green Limited Edition BROADCAST-AP / Blue Limited Run PG-24V-FS \u2013 rosso corsa BC-24V-USA PG-24V-FS \u2013 magenta PG-24V-FS \u2013 mint turquoise BC-24V-PG BC-24V-LTD STOCKISTS SOUNDS SUPPORT FAQs INTERNAL TRIMMERS POWER REQUIREMENTS WARRANTY PRIVACY POLICY WEEE Policy CONTACT CUSTOM ARCHIVED Home &pound; 0.00 0 items Home / PEDALS / BROADCAST LIMITED EDITIONS / BC-24V-USA BC-24V-USA AVAILABLE EXCLUSIVELY FROM OUR US STOCKISTS The BC-24V-USA runs internally at 24 volts from a standard 9 volt supply. The increased voltage gives extra headroom and a tighter low end \u2013 fantastic if you are looking for a little less saturation and grit, but without losing that unique sound of the Broadcast. The BC-24V-USA comes finished in turquoise-green and can only be purchased for a limited time through stockists located in the USA. The Broadcast is a transformer-coupled, discrete Class-A germanium circuit, that takes its inspiration from classic recording consoles of the 1960s. The unique way in which the circuit saturates and colours your signal can be used to produce biting clean boosts, subtly coloured and thickened signals with a frayed-at-the-edge quality or \u2013 when pushed \u2013 an individual sounding overdrive with a fuzzy, fried texture. The BC-24V-USA also features a three position gain switch offering MID-LOW-HIGH modes. In LOW mode, the pedal has most headroom and stays nearly clean across its range, whilst retaining colouration from its germanium circuit and transformer \u2013 perfect if you use higher output pickups, baritone, bass or keyboards . The MID mode is voiced to sound and behave as the regular Broadcast \u2013 still pretty clean but adding more grit and saturation to the mix. In HIGH mode, as with the regular Broadcast, the BC-24V-USA heads into overdrive, distortion and fuzz but with a slightly tighter low end. Categories: BROADCAST LIMITED EDITIONS , PEDALS Description FAQ Description Selected Germanium transistor TRIAD Magnetics steel-core transformer BI potentiometers Alpha Heavy duty footswitch (wired for true bypass) 3 position gain switch Individually hand-built on to a high-quality PCB, assembled, hand-wired, tested and packaged all by Michael Hudson LEVEL \u2013 Controls the overall volume of the pedal. GAIN SWITCH \u2013 Selects low, medium or high gain mode. GAIN TRIM \u2013 Controls the gain level of the Broadcast. At higher settings the high-end of the signal is gently rolled off. LOW CUT \u2013 Attenuates the low-end of the Broadcast. Since this control lies at the front end of the Broadcast\u2019s circuitry, it is interactive with the gain controls. IMPORTANT! THIS VERSION OF THE BROADCAST CONTAINS A VOLTAGE BOOSTER TO INCREASE THE VOLTAGE OF THE POWER SUPPLY UNIT FROM 9V UP TO 24V. DO NOT ATTEMPT TO RUN THIS PEDAL AT POWER SUPPLY VOLTAGES HIGHER THAN 9.6VDC AS THIS MAY DAMAGE THE PEDAL AND VOID ITS WARRANTY! DC SOCKET \u2013 The Broadcast requires a DC power supply unit (PSU). Please ensure your PSU can supply 9v, a minimum current of 50mA and has a 2.1mm negative centre barrel plug. Any other type may damage your pedal. If you plan on sharing the same PSU with other pedals, we recommend using a PSU with isolated outputs, e.g. Voodoo Lab PP2. CURRENT DRAW \u2013 50mA maximum   Content missing Related p